# Atari 2600 ROMs that are safe to redistribute.
#
# One canonical ROM filename per non-comment, non-blank line. Consumed by
# tools/roms/split-by-license.ts (which drops these comments before matching).
# Names are the canonical TOSEC-style names the sibling tools/roms/canonicalize.ts
# normalizes on-disk files to, so matching is exact.
#
# Every entry MUST carry a license citation above it justifying inclusion
# (B-0083 acceptance criteria; see tools/lint/no-empty-dirs.allowlist for the
# in-repo "reason comment per entry" precedent). Each ROM below is a homebrew
# release whose author explicitly permits free redistribution.

# Halo 2600 -- homebrew demake by Ed Fries (ex-Microsoft); released as a free
# download by the author. https://atariage.com/software_page.php?SoftwareLabelID=2008
Halo 2600 (2010) (Ed Fries).bin

# Anguna -- homebrew by Nathan Tolbert; free/open homebrew release.
# https://www.bytesizedgames.com/anguna2600.html
Anguna (2012) (Nathan Tolbert).bin

# Thrust -- homebrew port by Thomas Jentzsch; freely distributed by the author.
# https://atariage.com/software_page.php?SoftwareLabelID=921
Thrust (2000) (Thomas Jentzsch).bin

# Sheep It Up! -- homebrew by Dr. Ludos; released free by the author.
# https://drludos.itch.io/sheep-it-up
Sheep It Up! (2012) (Dr. Ludos).bin

# Duck Attack! -- homebrew by Will Nicholes; free download from the author.
# https://www.willnicholes.com/duckattack/
Duck Attack! (2010) (Will Nicholes).bin

# Jammed -- homebrew puzzle game by Chris Read; freely distributed homebrew.
# https://atariage.com/software_page.php?SoftwareLabelID=2168
Jammed (2009) (Chris Read).bin

# Star Battle -- homebrew by Scott Williamson; free homebrew release.
# https://atariage.com/software_page.php?SoftwareLabelID=1486
Star Battle (2006) (Scott Williamson).bin
